OL,3,GNEWSAAdventurer completes oceans row
OL,4,Aafter 327 days at sea
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former Royal Marine has completed a
OL,7,Fsolo and unsupported row across the
OL,8,FPacific and Indian Ocean, having not
OL,9,Fset foot on land for 327 days.
OL,11,FDave "Dinger" Bell, from Bere Regis,
OL,12,FDorset, set off from the west coast of
OL,13,FPeru on 9 November last year with 350
OL,14,Fdays worth of food and equipment on
OL,15,Fboard his carbon-fibre boat.
OL,17,FHe stepped ashore in Kilifi, north of
OL,18,FMombasa, Kenya, at 10:15 BST (12:15
OL,19,Flocal time) after rowing more than
OL,20,F15,000 nautical miles (28,000km).
